{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774728,"nonce":"AfQ+szM4jhLuMmAYNK7aDzOIGH4=","title":"fix: QA-sweep findings — matrix launch, per-Take retries, concurrency cancel, gate/cancel, service naming, UI Take-scoping","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #57 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/qa-findings` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-23T20:49:42Z · Merged: 2026-07-23T20:50:00Z\n\n\nFixes surfaced by a multi-operator QA sweep of the dogfood pipeline (reruns / retries / cancels / logs / outputs), each root-caused in code and adversarially verified. A recurring theme runs through several of them: **attempts and evidence must be Take-scoped** (ADR-0056), not billed against the flat cross-Take history.\n\n\n**Correctness (HIGH)**\n- **Cross-environment concurrency cancel** — a `production` dispatch silently cancelled an unrelated in-flight `staging` run. Two compounding defects: the `concurrency.group` was stored literally (never interpolated), and the environment newest-wins opt-out wasn't wired to the `cancel-in-progress` slot path. Now the group is interpolated at admission and governed deploys serialize without cancelling. (`b94ae65`)\n- **Matrix legs never ran** — `${{ matrix.* }}` was unresolved at launch (the engine `StepSpec` dropped `matrix_values` at the conversion boundary), so every matrix leg failed pre-launch with zero logs. Carried the coordinate through and bound `matrix` into the launch interpolation context. (`343555f`)\n- **Retries didn't happen on rerun** — the `retry: {max}` budget was counted over the flat cross-Take attempt history, so a leg that exhausted its retries in the original take never retried after a rerun. Now counted per-Take from the event log (order-based). (`04a97af`)\n\n**Correctness (MED / LOW-MED)**\n- **Shared-service pod-name collision on rerun** — service k8s resources were named take-agnostically, so a rerun's service pod collided with the terminating prior-take pod and never started (postgres showed `failed`). Names are now take-scoped. (`4e6915b`)\n- **Gate-approval on a skipped/terminal gate** returned `202 {released:true}` and appended a phantom `GateApproved`. Now rejected `409`; `released` is derived from the real transition; non-gate step returns a precise error. (`a1a009b`)\n- **Cancellation had no provenance** — added `RunCancelRequested{by}` so operator cancels are attributable and distinguishable from system/concurrency auto-cancels. (`a1a009b`)\n- **Workspace git ownership** — the executor now marks the provisioned `/workspace` git-trusted for every step (env-based config), so steps running as a different uid than the clone no longer hit \"dubious ownership\"; removed the per-pipeline band-aid. (`c785d40`, supersedes `be16ef9`)\n\n**UI (Take-scoping)**\n- **Step attempts** are now Take-scoped in the live view, not only when time-traveling. (`5fc817e`)\n- **Step duration** stopped growing across reruns — scoped to the selected take's attempts. (`a334ca4`)\n\n**Build**\n- Wrapped the web-ui entry in an async IIFE to avoid top-level await failing the production build. (`f64c5cc`)\n\n\nNew/updated hermetic tests (no Postgres/cluster): per-env concurrency + governed-serialize, matrix-coordinate-resolves-at-launch, gate/cancel guards, take-scoped service naming, and `author_retry_budget_resets_per_take_on_rerun`. UI changes typecheck + build clean.\n\n\n- Not yet verified end-to-end on a live cluster — recommend a dogfood run from this branch (matrix legs run, retries reset per take, per-take step time, postgres healthy). Reruns will now re-run failed `test` legs up to 3×/take again.\n- Repo-wide `cargo fmt` + machine-applicable clippy cleanup are on a **separate** branch (`chore/repo-wide-fmt`) to keep this PR focused; the dogfood `lint` step needs that branch to pass `cargo fmt --check`.\n- One deliberate follow-up: a launch-interpolation failure reason is still dropped (shows as a bare `step` failure) — surfacing it to the event/attempt grain needs a channel in the pure engine crate, left out of scope here.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}